# Button loading

Shared `Button` (`src/components/ui/Button.tsx`) already supports:

- `isLoading` — shows a spinner, disables the control, and shows a loading label

## Do

```tsx
<Button isLoading={mutation.isLoading} onClick={onPay}>
  Pay now
</Button>
```

- Bind `isLoading` to pending state so feedback starts on press (see `frontend-perceived-performance.mdc`)
- If a custom loading label is required, extend `Button` with `loadingText` rather than ternary children

## Don't

- Manual ternary children: `{loading ? "Saving..." : "Save"}`
- Separate `disabled={loading}` when `isLoading` already disables
- Custom spinners next to the button when the component handles it
- Waiting for the network before showing loading feedback
